# Seeded rules: default = TOKEN_BUCKET 5 per 10s, search = SLIDING_WINDOW_LOG 3 per 10s.
# Fastest demo from a terminal:
#   for i in {1..7}; do curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code} " -H 'x-client-id: alice' localhost:3000/limited/ping; done
#   -> 200 200 200 200 200 429 429
@base = http://localhost:3000

### Rules
GET {{base}}/rate-limits/rules

### Ping as alice (send 6 times quickly -> 6th is 429; see X-RateLimit-* and Retry-After headers)
GET {{base}}/limited/ping
x-client-id: alice

### Ping as bob -> own bucket, still 200
GET {{base}}/limited/ping
x-client-id: bob

### Search uses the 'search' rule (3 per 10s, sliding window)
GET {{base}}/limited/search?q=keka
x-client-id: alice

### Alice's allowance without spending it
GET {{base}}/rate-limits/usage/alice?rule=default

### Tighten the default rule (resets all buckets for it)
PATCH {{base}}/rate-limits/rules/default
Content-Type: application/json

{ "limit": 2, "windowMs": 5000 }

### New rule
POST {{base}}/rate-limits/rules
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "login", "algorithm": "SLIDING_WINDOW_LOG", "limit": 5, "windowMs": 60000 }

### Duplicate -> 409
POST {{base}}/rate-limits/rules
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "login", "algorithm": "TOKEN_BUCKET", "limit": 5, "windowMs": 60000 }

### Validation -> 400
POST {{base}}/rate-limits/rules
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "BAD KEY", "algorithm": "MAGIC", "limit": 0, "windowMs": 1 }

### Delete
DELETE {{base}}/rate-limits/rules/login
